The training observations show that the highest measured \(T_c\) values (102–137 K) belong exclusively to a few closely related cuprate families: Hg/Tl-1223 (and close n=3 analogues) containing Ba–Ca–Cu–O, (Cu,Tl)-12(n-1)n, and Pb-stabilized Bi-2223/2234. All other chemistries in the training set (YBCO-type, 2212, 1201, Fe-pnictides, borocarbides, alloys, MgB\(_2\), etc.) lie well below 95 K.

Applying the same compositional patterns to the pool immediately isolates six n\(\ge\)3 cuprates. The Sr-based Hg member (c084) is discarded because every Hg–Sr example in the training data has \(T_c\le\)64 K. The remaining five map directly onto the high-\(T_c\) training prototypes:

- c034 is a Tl–Ba–Ca–Cu–O multilayer (same elements as the 110–123 K Tl-22xx/12xx records);
- c029 is a (Cu,Ag)–1234 (same family as the 115 K training example);
- c046 is a Pb/Mo-stabilized Bi-2223 (identical to the 106–111 K records);
- c097 is essentially the exact Bi-2234 composition that measured 102.7 K;
- c081 is a higher-n Bi–Pb–Sr–Ca–Cu analogue of the 105 K mixed-layer record.

These five are therefore predicted to be the highest-\(T_c\) candidates, ranked by closeness of family and n to the very highest training examples.

Final: c034, c029, c046, c097, c081
